      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page ([[write-journal]]) describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n1. **Pre-write recording**: Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n2. **Rollback capability**: If an agent run fails (due to turn cap being exceeded, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content for files that existed, and deleting newly created files.\n\n3. **All-or-nothing semantics**: This mechanism gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without needing a database transaction\u2014the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of a single run.\n\n4. **Query agent note**: The Query agent doesn\u0027t use this rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5402,
      "output_tokens": 250
    }
